# Sandbox vs IDE runtime

Two AWS contexts. **No shared filesystem.**

1. **Firecracker sandbox** — agent execution, worktrees, publication exports.
   Use the real sandbox routes: `apps/web/app/api/workspaces/[workspaceId]/sandbox/**`.
2. **Orca IDE session** — one `orca serve` per workspace, embedded as a
   same-origin iframe. It has **no separate `/ide` route family** in
   `apps/web`. It talks to the parent over `postMessage`
   (`codev-bridge.ts` ↔ `components/codev-parent-bridge.ts`), which proxies to
   ordinary `/api/workspaces/{id}/...` endpoints (`presence`,
   `collaboration/conflicts`, `agents/{sessionId}/...`). The only literal
   `/ide` path is the orchestrator's `POST/GET /v1/sandboxes/{workspaceId}/ide`
   (Orca pairing/readiness) — that's `services/orchestrator`, not `apps/web`.

Do not write sandbox files expecting the IDE session to see them, or the
reverse. Web app = Vercel control plane. Do not move control-plane work into
AWS or IDE-session work onto Vercel serverless as a shortcut.
